;*******************************************************************
;* FTPSDATA - z/OS FTP client FTP.DATA statements for secure (FTPS)
;* outbound transfers from the Policy Administration System (PAS).
;*
;* Install as ACME.PAS.PARMLIB(FTPSDATA) and reference from batch JCL
;* with:  //SYSFTPD  DD DSN=ACME.PAS.PARMLIB(FTPSDATA),DISP=SHR
;*
;* The client certificate and the trusted CA certificates for the
;* destination hosts live in the RACF keyring named below; no key or
;* password material belongs in this member or in the JCL.
;*******************************************************************
;
; Negotiate TLS with AUTH TLS (explicit FTPS, RFC 4217) and fail the
; transfer rather than falling back to a cleartext session.
SECURE_MECHANISM          TLS
TLSMECHANISM              FTP
TLSRFCLEVEL               RFC4217
SECURE_FTP                REQUIRED
;
; Encrypt both the control connection (login, command stream) and the
; data connection (file contents).
SECURE_CTRLCONN           PRIVATE
SECURE_DATACONN           PRIVATE
;
; TLS 1.2 only, with forward-secret AES-GCM cipher suites.
TLSV1                     OFF
TLSV1.1                   OFF
TLSV1.2                   ON
CIPHERSUITE               TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384
CIPHERSUITE               TLS_ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256
;
; Client certificate and trusted CAs; SERVAUTH-protected RACF keyring
; owned by the batch service ID, not by an individual user.
KEYRING                   ACMEBTCH/PASFTPSRING
;
; Credentials are read from the RACF-protected NETRC dataset allocated
; by the job (//NETRC DD), so no user ID or password is embedded in the
; in-stream FTP command input.
